  "ownership": "Project-authored synthetic TST.L (xxx).L adversarial byte recipes for SEG-007-T009; no commercial content and no commercially derived bytes. Every image is constructed from the recipe recorded with it, and every opcode word used is an ordinary public Motorola encoding. The three accepted vectors carrying contract_recorded_sha256 reproduce docs/references/tst-l-absolute-long-contract.md's recorded accepted recipes verbatim so fixture drift is caught; every other vector is newly authored here as an adversarial superset of tests/fixtures/tst-l-fixtures.json, which this manifest never reads or modifies.",
  "recipe": "Each image is image_length bytes (hexadecimal) of 0x00, with every writes entry's uppercase hexadecimal bytes stored at its hexadecimal image offset; sha256 is the SHA-256 of exactly those constructed bytes. Every image places the instruction at the manifest-level entry_image_offset 0x100 with the manifest-level entry PC 0x00000100, except where a rejection entry carries its own entry_pc/entry_image_offset pair (identity-mapped, so both name the same source address) to reach a precedence step the manifest-level even entry address makes unreachable.",
